course: dictionary
lesson: 8100
title: Rebirth: the Renaissance and a renaissance
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from parts that give you clues. «The Renaissance, which means rebirth, began in Italy in the 1400s» tells you the word means rebirth, or coming back to life. So the Renaissance was a time when old ideas came back to life.
explain: Look at the capital letter. «The Renaissance was a period of new learning and art in Europe» names a time in history, so it has a capital R. Small r, as in «a renaissance», is a general word for a new burst of interest or energy in something, like a town or hobby that becomes popular again.
explain: Context helps you choose the right meaning. Ask yourself: does the sentence still make sense if you swap in your meaning? «Leonardo da Vinci, an Italian of the Renaissance, filled notebooks with drawings» still works with "a time of new learning", so you have the right meaning.
fact: The Renaissance was a time in Europe, from about the 1300s to the 1600s, when art, science and learning grew greatly.
fact: The Renaissance started in Italy, when thinkers got excited again about the learning of ancient Greece and Rome.
fact: Renaissance can be a noun for a time, or an adjective, as in Renaissance art.
fact: A renaissance (small r) is a new burst of interest or energy in something, a rebirth.
fact: A Renaissance man or woman is someone who is good at many things.
exercise: «The Renaissance was a period of new learning and art in Europe.» What was the Renaissance? | A new type of football | A toy car made in Italy | A kind of Italian pasta | *A time in history, from about the 1300s to the 1600s, when art and learning grew
exercise: «The Renaissance, which means rebirth, began in Italy.» What does rebirth mean? | A painting of a bird | *A new start, or coming back to life | A long sleep
exercise: «Leonardo da Vinci filled notebooks with drawings; most of his machines were never built.» What does this suggest? | He was a builder of bridges | Machines are dull to draw | *Many of his ideas were never made in real life | All his machines worked perfectly
test: The old station had a renaissance when local people painted it and held concerts there. What does renaissance mean here? | *A new burst of interest and life | Sleep | A broken-down building | A railway train
test: Someone good at painting, science and music is called a Renaissance man or woman. What does this mean? | *Good at many things | Lost in history | Very tall | Only good at one sport
exam: Why is «the Renaissance» written with a capital R, but «a renaissance» is not? | *Because the Renaissance is a named period of history, and small r is a general word for a new burst | Because it is a French word | Because it is the name of a person | Because it is at the start of a sentence in both
